# Data Architecture (Medallion Schema)

The PostgreSQL Data Warehouse is logically divided into three schemas managed by dbt:
1. `raw` (Bronze Layer): Landing zone for raw data extracted by Airflow. Strictly no transformations applied here.
2. `staging` (Silver Layer): Technical cleaning, data typing, and null removal.
3. `marts` (Gold Layer): Analytical models (Star Schema) ready to be connected to Metabase.